# mm.audio test target

Exercises the sample arithmetic at every width from one to thirty-two bits,
Ring's contract -- configure refusals, wrap at every offset for capacities that
are and are not powers of two, the zero-copy regions, full and empty, claims,
and loss counts -- and a producer and a consumer on two threads pushing a few
million samples through a small ring in order. It checks that Stream, In, and
Out answer honestly where nothing implements them, that a Stream other than a
Ring stands in for one, and that the selection pair returns what was
registered. No hardware and no platform provider are involved.
